<div class="content-box" style="background: #fff3cd; border-left: 4px solid #ffc107;">
    <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-lightbulb"></i> Watch Out For</h2>
    <p>Common misconceptions to avoid:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Direct Access: Students often try to "directly access" an element in a dynamic list using an index without realising that under the hood, some structures require sequential traversal.</li>
        <li>Static Size: Believing a static array can be resized if it gets "full."</li>
        <li>Stack/Queue Logic: Mixing up the end where data is added (e.g., trying to pop from the bottom of a stack).</li>
        <li>2D Indices: Confusing [row][column] order (remember: "RC Cola" or "Rows then Columns").</li>
    </ul>
</div>

